# CMS execution order (full batch & sequencing policy)

When the user says **Run CMS**, **`npm run test:cms`**, or **`npm run test:cms:headless:report`**, the repo runs **`scripts/run-cms-headless-background.sh`** (returns immediately; work continues under `nohup`), which invokes **`scripts/run-cms-headless-report.sh`** → **`scripts/run-cms-sequential-modules-dashboard.sh`**. Use **`npm run test:cms:foreground`** to run the same pipeline in the foreground. Do not use a single flat `Project=CMS` Playwright grep for full batches unless debugging.

## 1. Cross-module sequence (strict, one module at a time)

Run **`Project=CMS Module=<name> Stage=main`** in this order (skip if `projects/CMS/<name>` does not exist):

1. `environment`  
2. `language`  
3. `branches`  
4. `stack`  
5. `content-models`  
6. `releases`  
7. `global-field`  
8. `assets`  
9. `entries`  
10. `labels` — only when that folder exists; otherwise skipped automatically  
11. `json-rich-text-editor`  
12. `users-and-roles`  
13. `live-preview`  
14. **Remaining modules**: `content-modeling`, `search`, `security`, `tokens`, `webhook`, `workflows`, `taxonomy`, `visual-experience`

**After the `workflows` module step**, run the **publish rules serial chain** (grep: `publish rules chain \(serial\)`).

**After the `users-and-roles` module step**, run the **role lifecycle serial chain** (grep: `role lifecycle chain \(serial\)`).

## 2. Within each module — CRUD order

- Flow JSON is sorted globally in `tests/flows.spec.ts` (`flowOrder`, `crudLifecycleRank`, stable keys).
- For sequential CMS batches, **`CMS_SEQUENTIAL_MODULE_ORDER=1`** and **`CMS_CONTINUE_ON_FAIL=1`** (set by **`scripts/run-cms-sequential-modules-dashboard.sh`**). Then **`Project=CMS` + `Stage=main`** module buckets use **one test with `test.step` per flow** so **every URL still runs after a failure** (no `describe.serial` fail-fast skip). URLs still run **one after another** in CRUD sort order inside that batch (create/add before edit/update before move/import/export-style ids; **delete-like ids are excluded** from these runs — see §4).
- **`CMS_CONTINUE_ON_FAIL`** lets later URLs in the module run after a **hard fail** but **does not suppress** it: each execution error **still fails** its **`test.step`** and the **module batch test** fails when done, **rethrowing** the original error or an **`AggregateError`** when several flows fail; only **doc verification** mismatches stay **warning-only** (non-throwing) per **`core/executor.ts`**.

## 3. Retry pass (failed / timedOut / interrupted) — **before delete batch**

- Unless **`SKIP_RETRY=1`**, after **§1** completes (all main modules + both serial chains), scan **`playwright-parts/*.json`** with **`scripts/collectRetryFlowTitlesFromJson.ts --partsDir <dir> --exportShell`**.
- **`eval`** the printed `export` lines: **`CMS_RETRY_FLOW_IDS`** (comma-separated flow ids from failed `test.step` leaves and non-batched failures), **`CMS_RETRY_PUBLISH_CHAIN`**, **`CMS_RETRY_ROLES_CHAIN`**, and optionally **`PLAYWRIGHT_RETRY_GREP`** for title-based cases. **`--grep` alone cannot retry individual URLs** inside the continue-on-fail module batch (one Playwright test per module).
- Run **one** Playwright pass; save part as **`89-retry-before-delete.json`**. Use **`CMS_SEQUENTIAL_MODULE_ORDER=0`** for this pass (parallel speed). Pass **`--grep`** only when **`PLAYWRIGHT_RETRY_GREP`** is set.
- Unset retry env vars after the pass. **Then** run the delete batch (§4). **Do not** run retry after delete or after trash.

## 4. Delete flows — one batched pass (after main modules + optional retry)

Run **one** Playwright pass over **all** CMS tests whose titles match **`CMS_DELETE_FLOW_GREP`** in `run-cms-sequential-modules-dashboard.sh` (delete-a-*, bulk-delete-*, `delete-content-type`, `edit-or-delete-a-comment`, etc.).

Main module runs use **`--grep-invert`** that pattern so deletes never run during §1.

## 5. Trash — always last (among Playwright flow phases)

After the delete batch, run:

- **`Project=CMS Module=trash Stage=main`**

## 5b. CMS informational coverage (executable + doc list)

- **`.flow.json` with `"type": "informational"`** and **no steps**: the executor loads **`source`** in the browser (public doc; no login) so the URL runs in the same **module batch order** as other flows in that module.
- **`flows/CMS/docs.json`** URLs (not backed by a flow file): after trash, **`tests/docs.spec.ts`** runs with **`--grep "Docs Project=CMS"`** (HTTP + title checks). Set **`SKIP_CMS_DOCS_SPEC=1`** to skip.
- **`data/cms-urls.csv`** is rebuilt at the start of each batch (**`buildCmsUrlsCsv.ts`**: all CMS `*.flow.json` `source` values + **`flows/CMS/docs.json`**). **Background docs-audit** uses **`DOCS_URLS_CSV=data/cms-urls.csv`** so link/image/table audit is **CMS-scoped** (executable + informational URLs together).

## 6. Merge JSON, then docs audit (CMS URLs / broken links), reports, Slack, open dashboard

- **Single merge** of **`playwright-parts/*.json`** → **`flows-results.json`** (includes retry part if present, then delete batch, then trash). *Note:* `docs.spec` and docs-audit write separate artifacts (`docs-results.json`, audit dir); they are not part of this merge.
- Copy **`flows-results-cms.json`** before docs-audit if that backup step is still used.
- **Broken-links / docs quality audit for CMS** (part of **Run CMS** by default): unless **`SKIP_DOCS_AUDIT=1`**, docs-audit runs for CMS URLs. **Default:** **`DOCS_AUDIT_BACKGROUND=1`** — start **`run-docs-audit-background.sh`** early with **`DOCS_URLS_CSV=data/cms-urls.csv`** (separate **`AUDIT_REPORT_DIR`**, logs under main **`REPORT_DIR`**); main pipeline skips inline audit so flow reports and bundle finish without waiting on crawl. **`DOCS_AUDIT_BACKGROUND=0`** runs **`tests/docs-audit.spec.ts`** inline after merge with **`DOCS_AUDIT_PROJECT=CMS`** and **`DOCS_URLS_CSV`** defaulting to **`data/cms-urls.csv`** so results land in the same **`REPORT_DIR`** for Excel / dashboards.
- Generate Excel, `cms-dashboard.html`, shared dashboard, **`report-bundle/`**, unified report, **`urlRunSummaryAndSlack`**.
- Open **`report-bundle/index.html`** when **`OPEN_CMS_DASHBOARD≠0`** and `open` exists (macOS). **`SKIP_OPEN_DASHBOARD=1`** (e.g. from **`run-project-batch-background.sh`**) forces **`OPEN_CMS_DASHBOARD=0`** so the bundle is not auto-opened.

## 7. Checklist (always follow this order)

| Phase | What runs |
|--------|-----------|
| A | Main modules §1 — **non-delete** `Stage=main` only, **CRUD order** within module (**`CMS_CONTINUE_ON_FAIL`**: every URL runs; no serial fail-fast skip) |
| A2 | Publish rules chain (after workflows module) |
| A3 | Roles chain (after users-and-roles module) |
| B | **Retry** failed/timedOut/interrupted (`--exportShell` → **`CMS_RETRY_*`** env + optional **`PLAYWRIGHT_RETRY_GREP`**) — optional if `SKIP_RETRY=1` or nothing to retry |
| C | **Delete** batch (`CMS_DELETE_FLOW_GREP`) |
| D | **Trash** module |
| D2 | **`docs.spec`** CMS only (`flows/CMS/docs.json` HTTP checks) unless **`SKIP_CMS_DOCS_SPEC=1`** |
| E | **Merge** all `playwright-parts/*.json` once |
| F | **Docs audit** (default: background; use **`DOCS_AUDIT_BACKGROUND=0`** for inline in **`REPORT_DIR`**) + dashboards + bundle + Slack + open bundle — if background, audit may still be running after bundle opens; check **`docs-audit-background.log`** / **`AUDIT_REPORT_DIR`** |

## 8. Changing this policy

Update **`CMS_MAIN_MODULES`**, **`CMS_DELETE_FLOW_GREP`**, and phase order in **`scripts/run-cms-sequential-modules-dashboard.sh`**. Update **`tests/flows.spec.ts`** only if CRUD sort rules change. **Keep this `.mdc` in sync** with the script.
